From 0b7e19f0da20193c7f55603b04622b74afd03e32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Kirby <sophendoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:50:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Remote interface for other mods: read and update tasks,
 status lines, mod-owned subtasks, extra assignees, a change event

Other mods can now work with the list through remote.call("Todo-List", ...): read tasks (get_tasks, get_task),
add and update them (add_task, update_task), give a task a short status line under its title coloured by kind
(info, progress, attention, error, success), manage their own subtasks on a task without touching players'
(set_subtasks with an owner name), complete or reopen tasks, and register assignees that aren't players
(add_assignee: offered in the add and edit dialogs after the players). on_tasks_changed (its id from
get_event_ids) is raised after any change to the list, from the UI or a remote call, and not again while its
handlers run. Every call validates its input and returns false or nil instead of raising.

Documented in the README ("For mod authors: the remote interface"). Saves from 19.15.x load unchanged; nothing
looks different until a mod sets a status or registers an assignee.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013M2f33Xu7wX4LwMnJ4eHDJ
